  "problem": "Above65536 admitted world candidates, Native stable-sorts the complete list by distance, trims it, then sorts the retained cells by canonical XYZ. The first complete sort needs transient buffers and orders candidates that are immediately discarded.",
  "change": "Partition the deterministic total order (finite squared distance, then canonical Z/Y/X) at the existing cap, resize, and canonically sort only the retained candidates. The initial world traversal is already unique canonical Z/Y/X, so tie selection equals the old stable distance sort. Under/equal-cap caller behavior, source reads, permissions, payloads, radius and ABI remain unchanged.",
  "helper": "namespace ncmm_world {\n// Input is the unique finite-distance canonical Z/Y/X world traversal.\n// Stable distance sorting selects the same set as ordering by distance then\n// original canonical position. Partition that total order before sorting only\n// the retained set back into canonical order; no temporary sort buffer.\ntemplate<class Candidate> void retain_nearest_candidates(std::vector<Candidate> &candidates,size_t maximum){\n    if(candidates.size()<=maximum)return;\n    std::nth_element(candidates.begin(),candidates.begin()+maximum,candidates.end(),[](const auto &a,const auto &b){\n        if(a.distance!=b.distance)return a.distance<b.distance;\n        return order(a.world)<order(b.world);\n    });\n    candidates.resize(maximum);\n    std::sort(candidates.begin(),candidates.end(),[](const auto &a,const auto &b){return order(a.world)<order(b.world);});\n}\n}\n",
  "correctness": {
    "private_checks": 576,
    "private_selected_payloads": 7375656,
    "repository_selected_payloads": 5531742,
    "negative_controls": 2,
    "cases": "Empty/small/under/equal/over65536/up to32*97*97, caps0/49/65536/greater than input, radial/random/ordered/reverse/equal/banded distances, signed zero, full world and opaque payload preservation.",
    "negative_control_repair": "The old all-equal distance-only nth_element control happened to preserve input order in MSVC and was not distinguishable. Replaced with an explicit reversed tie order in a mixed-distance boundary. Both reversed ties and missing final XYZ order are now rejected."
